comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T21:41:33.254Z",codex-root,"History-completeness audit 2026-07-13: before this audit mutated the tracker, all 1,792 discovered history streams and all 28,195 events were read; integrity checks found zero missing streams, unreadable logs, hash mismatches, chain mismatches, or history drift. Item mutation integrity is therefore currently healthy. Keep this item open because workspace-scoped configuration, schema, profile, initialization, and other non-item mutation paths still need explicit immutable audit coverage and restoration semantics, coordinated with pm-klo8."
  "2026-07-24T05:17:57.275Z",claude-code-agent,"Investigation evidence: the current repository has multiple overlapping mutation inventories (CLI registration families, migration write gates, telemetry roots, MCP action contracts). A truthful contract-driven execute-every-mutation gate requires first consolidating those sources into one executable registration contract; this PR does not pretend a static scope list satisfies that acceptance criterion. Returning this item to open while the three fully implemented mutation-integrity items remain active."
  "2026-07-24T22:21:52.156Z",claude-code-agent,"Partial implementation evidence: PM_MUTATION_ACTION_CONTRACTS now provides one public typed classification of core mutation actions and required item/workspace history scopes, with drift tests and SDK documentation. This does not yet satisfy the item acceptance criterion to execute every classified mutation against a sandbox and assert op/author, so the item will return to open rather than being falsely closed."
  "2026-07-24T22:26:09.585Z",claude-code-agent,"Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/684"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T17:55:54.464Z","harness:claude-code","Live measurement of the two gate scopes, 2026-07-25, so the phased acceptance criteria can be checked against real numbers rather than an assumed inventory.\n\nItem scope (phase 1) — 30 distinct ops appear across the 2,031 per-item history streams (34,160 entries total): comment_add 7,096, update 5,992, files_add 5,948, tests_add 2,759, claim 2,429, close 1,990, create 1,989, release 1,958, docs_add 1,243, test_run_track 733, learning_add 571, note_add 563, update_audit 309, append 114, plan_complete_step 85, plan_add_step 71, plan_update_step 44, history_compact_baseline 41, history_compact 41, history_repair 35, update_ownership_bypass 29, history_redact 21, plan_create_metadata 19, plan_create_initial_step 12, plan_append_discovery 12, plan_append_validation 9, delete 9, plan_append_decision 7, plan_approve 6, plan_link_step 4.\n\nThat observed set is the ground truth the contract enumeration must cover, and it is a useful cross-check in both directions: an op that appears here but is not enumerated by the mutation tables means the tables are incomplete, and an enumerated mutating action that never appears here is either dead or untested by dogfooding (which pm-pww8ax now tracks as a capability-coverage question).\n\nWorkspace scope (phase 2) — the mechanism exists and is barely used. `.agents/pm/history/_workspace.jsonl` holds exactly 9 entries, all with op `history:author-acknowledge`. No entry records a settings, schema, profile, init, or extension-state mutation, which confirms the phase-2 boundary this item already declares: workspace-scope mutations are today entirely outside the append-only proof, not merely partially covered.\n\nTwo consequences worth carrying into the acceptance criteria. First, the known-unaudited allowlist for phase 1 can be seeded from the diff between the enumerated tables and the 30 observed ops, so it starts honest rather than empty. Second, because `_workspace.jsonl` already exists and carries a hash chain, phase 2 is a matter of routing existing mutations into it rather than designing a new stream — which makes the phase-2 gate cheaper than the phasing note implies, and worth reconsidering as part of pm-klo8 rather than after it."
